From b28adff54923825eeda96ee52e5c38042d71d257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:07:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the online mod on Sonic Riders Tournament Edition
 (GXSRTE 2.4.6.1)

srnp_game.hpp/.cpp: the game that runs (the disc's ID at boot); At(us), a Sonic Riders US address in it
(srnp_game_te.inc: 760 ranges made from the two games' code by tools/srnp/te: code matched by the
instructions' shape, data by the instructions that compute their addresses; the REL's BSS moved as one
block, -0xD66C0; a racer the same 0x1080 bytes); InGame, the mod's words for TE (a branch to its
target's place, the same instruction's immediate carried over from TE's).

srnp_racers.cpp: memory through At; patches by Resolve/Made/SwapIn (TE's original read and checked by
its shape); the caves holding addresses made for the game; seats 5-7 on TE, where the racers' low half
goes past 0x7FFF, through three-word caves in free low memory (0x80002010-0x80002A00); TE's race setup
(its Free Race keeps the racer count at 1 while the menu writes the racers), its gear table (44, the
Chaos Emerald for Super Sonic only: Sonic on it hangs the loading), two more sound handles out of the
checksum (+0xF60), racer 0 always drawn on TE (left out, TE changed scene). srnp_relay.cpp: the state's
hash, rules, task pool (TE's held at 0x8042E58C), main loop hook (TE's 0x8027B934) by game. The waiting
screen: TE's characters' names, a greyish green background on TE (Gibax). Labels 5P-8P: not on TE yet.

Measured on 2026-11-26 (native, TE's module): 2 runners 0 divergence; 8 runners, Sonic, Metal Sonic,
Blaze, Tikal, Silver, Chaos, Super Sonic, Shadow: the seat 7 case fixed and checked on 2 runners
(43 identical, 0 divergence).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
